{"name":"Warm Waterlogged Lab Coat","hex":"#a89a8c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"warm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a somewhat high temperature, often but not always connoting that the high temperature is pleasant rather than uncomfortable.","Friendly and with affection."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make or keep warm.","To become warm, to heat up."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warm"},{"term":"waterlogged","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Soaked with water.","In danger of sinking because of excess water onboard."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/waterlogged"},{"term":"lab","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-3 language code for Linear A."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A laboratory.","Laboratory experiment, test, investigation or result."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lab"}],"entries":[{"title":"White coat","blocks":[{"text":"A white coat, also known as a laboratory coat, lab gown, or lab coat, is a knee-length overcoat or smock worn by professionals in the medical field or by those involved in laboratory work. The coat protects their street clothes and also serves as a simple uniform. The garment is made from white or light-colored cotton, linen, or cotton polyester blend, allowing it to be washed at high temperature and making it easy to see if it is clean."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/42/Forskerspirer_fra_By%C3%A5sen_videreg%C3%A5ende_skole_%286188348946%29.jpg/330px-Forskerspirer_fra_By%C3%A5sen_videreg%C3%A5ende_skole_%286188348946%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_coat"},{"title":"Coat","blocks":[{"text":"A coat is an outer garment for the upper body, worn by any gender for warmth or fashion. Coats typically have long sleeves and are open down the front, and closing by means of buttons